    "Answer A (Gap Year if Structured Default): Take a gap year if you have a clear plan \u2014 structured gap years (work abroad, volunteering, skill building) produce higher GPA and major satisfaction, and most universities support deferral.",
    "Answer B (Start University Immediately): Go straight to university if you don't have a specific gap year purpose \u2014 unstructured gap years rarely produce meaningful growth and risk undermining academic momentum without a clear plan.",
    "Answer C (Gap Year for Career Clarity): Take a gap year specifically to explore different career environments if you're undecided about your major \u2014 a year of deliberate career testing before committing to a program reduces costly mid-degree changes."
